  "articleBody": "Picking the perfect tile for your bathroom can feel a little daunting, but it doesn't have to be! Let's break down what you should think about. First off, because bathrooms are wet, you absolutely need to consider the tile's slip resistance, especially for floors. Safety first, right? Then, think about durability and how much water the tile absorbs – some tiles are better suited for high-moisture areas like showers than others. The size and layout of the tile can totally change the feel of your bathroom, so visualize how it'll look. Maintenance is another big factor; do you want something super easy to clean, or are you okay with a bit more upkeep? Don't forget about grout color – it really impacts the final look! When you're talking to installers, ask if they include substrate repair and proper waterproofing in their quotes. This stuff is super important to prevent issues down the line. If you’re revamping a shower or dealing with tricky large-format tiles, a pro can ensure everything is done right to avoid hidden water damage. HH Remodeling in the Denver area can help you navigate these choices for a beautiful and lasting bathroom.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
